  {
   "id": "flower-fundamentals",
   "src": "bde-section-258-141",
   "heading": "Flower Fundamentals",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "html": "Cannabis flower is where it all begins—aromatic, potent, and packed with personality. From Indica to Sativa, THC to terpenes, understanding the basics can help you find the right strain and experience for your needs. This guide breaks down everything you need to know to shop smart and smoke confidently."
    },
    {
     "type": "faq",
     "items": [
      {
       "q": "Indica, Sativa, Hybrid",
       "a_html": "<p>These classic categories are a helpful starting point for understanding how different cannabis strains might make you feel.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Alternative Cannabinoids",
       "a_html": "<p>There’s more to cannabis than just THC. Compounds like CBD, CBN, THCV, and CBG each bring their own unique effects—helping with everything from sleep to focus to stress relief. Exploring these cannabinoids can help you personalize your cannabis experience.</p>"
      },
      {
       "q": "Extraction, Hash, Live Resin & Rosin",
       "a_html": "<p>Cannabis concentrates come in many forms, each offering a more potent, flavorful, or refined version of the plant. From traditional hash to modern extracts like live resin and rosin, these products deliver strong effects with a smaller dose.</p>"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "headingLevel": 2
  },
  {
   "id": "the-3-classic-flower-categories-indica-sativa-hybrid",
   "src": "bde-section-258-151",
   "heading": "The 3 Classic Flower Categories: Indica, Sativa Hybrid",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "img",
     "src": "/assets/photos/ll/ladyl_iconography_flower.webp",
     "alt": "LadyL_Iconography_Flower",
     "orig": "https://ladyljerseycity.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LadyL_Iconography_Flower.webp",
     "w": 500,
     "h": 500
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "html": "Most modern, commercially produced cannabis no longer fits neatly into traditional strain categories, due to widespread hybridization and the infusion of edibles."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "html": "Still, these classic categories—Indica, Sativa, and Hybrid—remain helpful for describing the general effects people can expect."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "html": "Cannabis products like flower, concentrates, and vapes are often labeled as Indica-leaning, Sativa-leaning, or Hybrid to reflect their typical effects."
    },
    {
     "type": "img",
     "src": "/assets/photos/ll/ladyl_iconography_indica_v2.webp",
     "alt": "LadyL_Iconography_Indica_V2",
     "orig": "https://ladyljerseycity.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/LadyL_Iconography_Indica_V2.webp",
     "w": 1500,
     "h": 1500
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "html": "For pain relief, <strong>relaxation</strong> and all other feelings related to being <strong>stoned</strong>."
    },
    {
